<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Topic//EN" "topic.dtd">
<topic id="git-addon-staged-files-area">
  <title>Stage Changes for Commit</title>
  
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <indexterm>Git Client add-on<indexterm>staged files</indexterm></indexterm>
        <indexterm>Git Client add-on<indexterm>commits</indexterm></indexterm>
      </keywords>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
  <body>
    <p id="p_qxw_wny_kpb">The <uicontrol>Staged files</uicontrol> area lists the resources that are
      ready to be committed. Stage only the files that belong in the next commit. You can unstage
      files and send them back to the <xref
        href="git-addon-unstaged-files-area.dita#git-addon-unstaged-files-area" format="dita"><uicontrol>Unstaged
          files</uicontrol> area</xref> if you decide not to include them. This area has actions
      similar to the <uicontrol>Unstaged files</uicontrol> area, except for <xref
        href="git-addon-actions-branches-history.dita#git-addon-actions-branches-history/action_show_history"><uicontrol>Show
          history</uicontrol></xref> and <xref
        href="git-addon-actions-branches-history.dita#git-addon-actions-branches-history/action_show_blame"><uicontrol>Show
          blame</uicontrol></xref>.</p>
  </body>
</topic>